    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d144">

                <pb facs="0289" n="157" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg157"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EW/5–2945</note>
                <head>No. 144 <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Balfour</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-05-29">May 29th, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Under Secretary</hi>:—In his telegram
                    no. 40 to the President,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d144-f1"/> Mr. Churchill mentioned that H. M. G. were drawing up, as the President desired,
                    a suggested list of subjects for discussion at the next meeting of Heads of
                    Governments. Mr. Eden has now asked me to
                    forward you the enclosed list of suggested topics.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d144-f2"
                    /> I expect you will wish to inform the President.</p>
                <p>Yours very sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Balfour</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d144-f1" n="1" xml:id="d144-f1-content">
